  "conclusion": "REDUCED-ROUND ONLY: deviations were detected only for reduced-round variants. These say nothing about full 64-round SHA-256/SHA-256d and give no mining advantage; full-round configurations (where tested) showed no deviation. Start nonce: optimal weights by rounds after entry [\"0\", \"11\", \"38\", \">=50\"]; last round reached at measured probability >= 2^-32: round 4; largest searched: 4 rounds, weight 50 (timeout). Start time-nonce: optimal weights by rounds after entry [\"0\", \"11\", \"38\", \">=39\"]; last round reached at measured probability >= 2^-32: round 4; largest searched: 4 rounds, weight 39 (timeout). Identities (all templates): 4-round H7 - bswap(nonce) constant: proved; 5-round H7 formula: proved.",
